# The platform-served asset class (usability F2): /assets/* files are
# edge-served by the Workers Static Assets handler (wrangler.jsonc assets
# block, assets-first/worker-on-miss) and never touch the Worker, so the
# security-headers middleware (src/web/security-headers.ts) cannot stamp
# them. This file is that class's header layer — the same mechanism the
# smoke-verified cache-control posture rides (findings-latency-health.md:
# assets immutable 1y). The catch-all carries upstream's tree-wide
# X-Content-Type-Options default (routers/common/middleware.go:48-64,
# modules/setting/security.go:28); X-Frame-Options rides too for the same
# "every response that leaves Gitea" coverage.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/.vite/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/assets/emoji.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/assets/licenses.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
